cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "ghost-qa: Autonomous Headless Browser QA & Self-Healing Verification Loop for AI Coding Agents"
abstract: >-
  ghost-qa is an autonomous headless browser verification CLI and installable
  AI agent skill. It crawls a running web application on desktop and mobile
  viewports, safely exercises interactive controls, and traps runtime
  failures (console and hydration errors, network failures, layout overflow,
  accessibility defects, and performance problems), returning a structured
  self-healing diagnostic that coding agents (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex,
  Cursor, Windsurf) use to fix their own defects before reporting task
  completion. It is available both as a CLI (npx ghost-qa) and as a native
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
authors:
  - name: "VibeFoundry"
